  "title": "1980 Portuguese legislative election",
  "summary": "A legislative election was held on 5 October 1980, ten months after the last one, because the December 1979 ballot had only filled out the legislature elected in 1976, which the constitution ran to 14 October 1980. The Democratic Alliance won again and Francisco Sá Carneiro stayed in office; he was killed in the Camarate air crash two months later, on 4 December, and Francisco Pinto Balsemão took the government. It is in the atlas as the majority that carried the constitutional revision of 1982 — the first legislature of the new regime to run its full course, and the one that removed the military tutelage from the constitution.",
